Day 7 — Network Analysis & Sniffing 🔎

Today I learned the fundamentals of network analysis and packet sniffing, focusing on how security professionals inspect network traffic and identify suspicious activity.

Topics Covered
Command-Line Network Analysis Tools
Network Sniffers
tcpdump — capturing and analyzing packets from the command line
Wireshark — graphical packet analysis and protocol inspection
Understanding how packet captures can help identify suspicious connections, protocols, and network behavior

Cybersecurity News — CSS Attacks on Webmail

I also studied new research showing how malicious CSS/HTML inside emails can escape the email's boundaries and interact with webmail interfaces.

Researchers demonstrated techniques affecting services such as Outlook, Gmail, Yahoo, AOL, Fastmail, and Proton Mail that could potentially be used to:

Steal passwords and authentication tokens
Manipulate trusted UI elements
Exfiltrate sensitive information
Abuse AI tools connected to email
Track when emails are opened
🔐 Key Takeaway

Day 7 connected network analysis with real-world security research: packet-analysis tools like Wireshark and tcpdump help security professionals investigate the network activity that can occur during attacks and data exfiltration.

